{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>But the field, when it goes out in the Jubilee.</b> It is stated in Torat Kohanim that 'field' is masculine, and it requires explanation for its interpretation. And do we not know that 'field' is mentioned everywhere in the masculine? Rather, this is what it says: that 'the field' is in the masculine clarifies the latter part of this verse, which is written לכהן תהיה אחוזתו. And as it concludes there: from where do you say of a field that goes out to the priests in the Jubilee? As it is written או אל אחד מבניו הכהנים והרי היא תחת ידו — and from where that it is as though it is his? As it concludes there in Arakhin: 'In the case of others' property I acquire; in my own, not all the more so?' Scripture says לכהן תהיה אחוזתו — and it does not depart to the priests [in perpetuity]. But since 'field' is mentioned in the masculine, if it referred back to 'field,' it should have written יהיה אחוזתו."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:43.802565064Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}